# Bluegrass Rhythm and the G Run (repertoire plan: st-bluegrass-g-run). An original 16-bar rhythm
# study in G: two 8-bar phrases on G (320003), C (x32010) and D (xx0232). Every bar is bass on
# beats 1 and 3, a down-strum of strings 4 to 1 on beats 2 and 4. Bass notes: G alternates string 6
# fret 3 (G) and the open string 4 (D); C alternates string 5 fret 3 (C) and string 6 fret 3 (G);
# D alternates the open string 4 (D) and the open string 5 (A). Before each C the G bar puts
# string 5 fret 2 (B) on beat 3, so the bass steps up B to C.
# Each phrase ends with the G run in eighth notes (bars 7 and 15): bass on 1, a short strum on 2,
# then the open string 3 (G), string 4 fret 2 (E), the open string 4 (D), the open string 5 (A)
# with a hammer-on to fret 2 (B), landing on string 6 fret 3 (G) on beat 1 of the next bar.
# Pick the run strictly down-up: up on the "and" of 2, down on 3, up, down on 4, and the hammer-on
# needs no pick. In the run, finger 1 takes string 4 fret 2, finger 2 hammers string 5 fret 2 and
# finger 3 lands on string 6 fret 3: the G chord is back under your hand. G is fingered 3-2-4
# (6:3, 5:2, 1:3); for C, fingers 3 and 2 each move one string toward the floor and finger 1 adds
# string 2 fret 1.
title: Bluegrass Rhythm and the G Run
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original rhythm study in the bluegrass style
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: bluegrass, boom-chick, g run, bass run, flatpicking, hammer-on
tempo: 120
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Your part
role: rhythm
